<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Jesus is true God and true man; in him is the salvation of humanity found.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that Jesus is true God, consubstantial with the Father (CCC 464-465).</li>
<li>Recognize that Jesus is true man, like us in all things but sin (CCC 470-471).</li>
<li>Understand the hypostatic union: two natures (divine and human) in one Person (CCC 467-468).</li>
<li>Discover the mystery of the kenosis: God emptied himself for love of us (CCC 471-472).</li>
<li>Inspire personal confession of faith: "But what about you? Who do you say I am?" (Mk 8:29).</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> "Who, being in very nature God, did not consider equality with God something to be used to his own advantage, but made himself nothing" (Phil 2:6-7)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 422-483</p>

</section>

